{"_id": "26722081|None", "id": "26722081", "infons": {}, "passages": [{"infons": {"journal": "Anticancer Res. 2016 Jan;36(1):455-60.", "year": "2016", "type": "title", "authors": "Fiala O, Pesek M, Finek J, Minarik M, Benesova L, Sorejs O, Svaton M, Bortlicek Z, Kucera R, Topolcan O"}, "offset": 0, "text": "Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor Gene Amplification in Patients with Advanced-stage NSCLC.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "3", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor", "locations": [{"offset": 0, "length": 32}]}, {"id": "4", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "Patients", "locations": [{"offset": 55, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "5", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "NSCLC", "locations": [{"offset": 84, "length": 5}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"type": "abstract"}, "offset": 91, "text": "BACKGROUND: Tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs) targeting epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) represent novel, effective tools in the management of advanced-stage non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). We aimed to evaluate the incidence and predictive role of EGFR gene amplification in patients with advanced-stage NSCLC treated with EGFR-TKIs. PATIENTS AND METHODS: The study included 290 patients with advanced-stage (IIIB or IV) NSCLC. Multiplex ligation-dependent probe amplification (MLPA) and polymerase chain reaction (PCR) were used for detection of EGFR gene amplification and EGFR mutations, respectively. RESULTS: EGFR amplification was detected in 26 (9.0%) patients. EGFR amplification was found more frequently in patients harboring the EGFR mutation (p<0.001). No significant corelation between EGFR gene amplification and survival was observed. CONCLUSION: EGFR gene amplification is associated with EGFR gene mutation. EGFR gene amplification is not a feasible predictive biomarker for treatment with EGFR-TKIs in patients with advanced-stage NSCLC.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "32", "infons": {"identifier": "7294", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2497", "valid": true, "normalized": [7294], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 7294, "biotype": "gene", "name": "TXK", "accession": "@GENE_TXK"}, "text": "Tyrosine kinase", "locations": [{"offset": 103, "length": 15}]}, {"id": "33", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "epidermal growth factor receptor", "locations": [{"offset": 147, "length": 32}]}, {"id": "34", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 181, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "35", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "non-small cell lung cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 256, "length": 26}]}, {"id": "36", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "